All of the polymorph restrictions seem to hinge on the usage of charges
   and the number of objects polymorphed with a single zap.  (Of course.)

So why not incorporate that into the code?  More specifically, if you 
   polymorph a pile of stuff, you use up 1 charge for each n objects 
   polymorphed, rounding up.  So that way, you can still zap yourself,
   your pet, or that dragon corpse for a net use of 1 charge, while 
   zapping at that pile of 400 rocks would drain the wand as fast as you
   could say "400 pieces of worthless yellowish-brown glass."  Probably
   faster.

This even fits in (kinda) with the spirit of the game.  A higher-level spell
   takes more mana points to cast (or am I misusing a moria term?), so
   shouldn't a mass polymorph require more charges?


